  "title": "DODD vs Aging Waiver in Ohio: Which Program Do You Qualify For?",
  "summary": "Trying to get Medicaid waiver support in Ohio? The first step is figuring out which system you belong to. Ohio has two separate waiver tracks: DODD waivers for people with developmental disabilities that started before age 22, and aging waivers (like PASSPORT) for older adults or people with disabilities acquired later in life. Applying to the wrong system can cost you months of time. This guide explains the key differences, who qualifies for what, and which agency to contact first.",
